I think almost all those would be nice, though I disagree about the
poison/no eat because in nature it doesn't work that way. Many venoms
are protein based--such as snakes. You can eat a venomous snake, you
can even drink it's venom and as long as you don't have an open sore in
your mouth or an ulcer in your stomach, it won't harm you.

The "poison" used in the pods of poison arrows that hunters use today
are nicotine based. It caused the blood vessels to constrict, animal
dies. Immediately following, you can eat the meat. Thus, I vote for
poisoned meat staying edible.



